# BookWriter — line endings, diff behaviour and binary classification.
#
# Why this file exists: this repo is developed on Windows (core.autocrlf=true)
# but deploys to Linux containers. Without explicit rules, a fresh Windows
# checkout renders update.sh with CRLF, turning its shebang into "#!/bin/bash\r"
# and breaking it the moment it reaches the server. Everything below that a
# container or a Linux host reads is pinned to LF regardless of the developer's
# local git config; everything Windows-only is pinned to CRLF. Nothing is left
# to autocrlf.
#
# Changing a rule here changes what lands in working trees on the next checkout,
# not what is stored in git. After editing, run:
#     git add --renormalize .
# and inspect `git status` before committing.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Default: normalize every text file to LF in the repository. Git detects
# text vs binary; the sections below override the detection where it matters.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
*                       text=auto

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# LF required — consumed by Linux, Docker or nginx. CRLF here is a live defect,
# not a cosmetic one.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Shell scripts. update.sh is the concrete case: CRLF breaks the shebang.
*.sh                    text eol=lf
*.bash                  text eol=lf

# Docker. Older non-BuildKit builders mis-parse a "\" line continuation
# followed by CR; the ignore file is read line-wise the same way.
Dockerfile              text eol=lf
Dockerfile.*            text eol=lf
*.dockerfile            text eol=lf
.dockerignore           text eol=lf

# Compose and any other YAML — read inside containers and by compose itself.
*.yml                   text eol=lf
*.yaml                  text eol=lf

# nginx and supervisord configs, baked into the image.
*.conf                  text eol=lf

# Env templates. The server's .env is sourced by compose and by shell.
.env.example            text eol=lf
*.env                   text eol=lf

# Python — the backend runs on Linux in the container.
*.py                    text eol=lf
*.pyi                   text eol=lf
*.toml                  text eol=lf
*.cfg                   text eol=lf
requirements*.txt       text eol=lf

# Frontend sources and assets served by nginx.
*.ts                    text eol=lf
*.tsx                   text eol=lf
*.js                    text eol=lf
*.jsx                   text eol=lf
*.mjs                   text eol=lf
*.cjs                   text eol=lf
*.css                   text eol=lf
*.scss                  text eol=lf
*.html                  text eol=lf
*.json                  text eol=lf

# Docs and dotfiles.
*.md                    text eol=lf diff=markdown
*.txt                   text eol=lf
.gitignore              text eol=lf
.gitattributes          text eol=lf
.gitkeep                text eol=lf
LICENSE                 text eol=lf

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# CRLF required — Windows-only tooling. start.ps1 and build.ps1 never run
# anywhere else, and .bat/.cmd genuinely misbehave with LF.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
*.ps1                   text eol=crlf
*.psm1                  text eol=crlf
*.psd1                  text eol=crlf
*.bat                   text eol=crlf
*.cmd                   text eol=crlf

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Diff drivers — better hunk headers when reviewing.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
*.py                    diff=python
*.html                  diff=html
*.css                   diff=css

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Generated / vendored — keep them out of diffs and out of language stats,
# but still merge-resolvable. package-lock.json is ~197 KB of noise in a review.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
package-lock.json       text eol=lf -diff linguist-generated
frontend/dist/**        linguist-generated

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Binary — never diffed, never line-ending-converted. The JSONL export/import
# artifacts and the SQLite + LanceDB data files matter most here: a CRLF
# rewrite would corrupt them.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
*.gz                    binary
*.jsonl.gz              binary
*.zip                   binary
*.7z                    binary
*.tar                   binary
*.db                    binary
*.sqlite                binary
*.sqlite3               binary
*.lance                 binary
*.png                   binary
*.jpg                   binary
*.jpeg                  binary
*.gif                   binary
*.ico                   binary
*.webp                  binary
*.pdf                   binary
*.woff                  binary
*.woff2                 binary
*.ttf                   binary
*.otf                   binary
*.eot                   binary

# SVG is text — keep it diffable, just pin the ending.
*.svg                   text eol=lf
